<section id="problem" class="studio-problem reference-section" data-tone="light"><div class="wrap studio-two"><div><span class="eyebrow">01 · THE PROBLEM</span><h2 class="reading-statement" data-reading>A high score can hide a shortcut.</h2><p class="statement-answer">When a dataset mostly contains one joint, a model can use cues such as framing or image dimensions to guess the joint. Compare predictions from checkpoints trained with and without FracAtlas.</p></div><div class="pixel-specimen"><img src="{{sample_file}}" alt="FracAtlas radiograph from specimen {{sample_number}}" width="{{sample_width}}" height="{{sample_height}}" loading="lazy"><span class="spec-tag tag-one">Pooled · {{prediction}}</span><span class="spec-tag tag-two">No FracAtlas · {{shift_prediction}}</span><span class="spec-tag tag-three">Confidence ≠ correctness</span><span class="pixel-caption">ONE IMAGE. DIFFERENT TRAINING.</span></div></div></section>
<section id="decides" class="decision-section reference-section" data-tone="volt"><div class="wrap"><span class="eyebrow">02 · HOW IT WORKS</span><div class="decision-heading"><h2>Every result<br><em>shows its context.</em></h2><div class="confidence-hero"><b>{{confidence}}<span>%</span></b><p>pooled softmax confidence<br>on this saved example.<br><strong>Not probability of correctness.</strong></p></div></div><div class="decision-cards"><article class="primary-receipt"><header><span class="receipt-code">E0</span><div><h3>Pooled checkpoint</h3><p>EfficientNet-B3 · all six sources · seed 0</p></div><span class="best-badge">SAME IMAGE</span></header><div class="receipt-spec"><img src="{{sample_file}}" alt="FracAtlas radiograph from specimen {{sample_number}}" width="{{sample_width}}" height="{{sample_height}}"><div><span>SPECIMEN {{sample_number}} · FRACATLAS</span><strong>{{prediction}}</strong><p>{{confidence}}% softmax confidence</p></div></div><div class="receipt-breakdown"><div><span>Input</span><b>Greyscale · 160 × 160</b></div><div><span>Task</span><b>Hip / Knee / Shoulder</b></div><div><span>Activation view</span><b>Pooled-model Grad-CAM</b></div><div><span>Data handling</span><b>In memory · no image storage</b></div></div><a href="demo.html?sample={{sample_number}}">Run this specimen in the workbench →</a><p class="receipt-caveat">{{sample_note}}</p></article><div class="other-receipts">{{checkpoint_receipts}}<div class="why-card"><span>WHY FOUR CHECKPOINTS?</span><p>The input stays the same. The training sources change. Compare the effect directly.</p></div></div></div></div></section>
<section id="lab" class="lab-section reference-section" data-tone="light"><div class="wrap"><span class="eyebrow">03 · THE LAB</span><h2>Same X-ray.<br><em>Different perspectives.</em></h2><div class="lab-intro"><p>Choose a joint to switch the specimen. These are saved outputs from the actual project checkpoints. Open the workbench to run live inference or upload your own image.</p><a class="btn primary" href="demo.html">Replay it in the Lab →</a></div><div class="lab-summary"><div><b>4</b><small>checkpoints compared</small></div><div><b>3</b><small>target joint classes</small></div><div><b>9</b><small>held-out examples</small></div><div><b>0</b><small>uploaded images stored</small></div></div><div class="xray-lab"><div class="lab-viewer"><div class="lab-viewer-top"><span>RADIOGRAPH / <b id="lab-specimen-id">02</b></span><span id="lab-recorded">RECORDED LABEL · HIP</span></div><div class="lab-film" id="lab-film"><img id="lab-xray" src="assets/samples/sample2.jpg" alt="Selected project radiograph" width="450" height="450"><div class="lab-scan" aria-hidden="true"></div><span class="lab-view-caption">ACTUAL SPECIMEN · SAVED CHECKPOINT OUTPUTS</span></div><div class="joint-picker" role="group" aria-label="Choose an X-ray example"><button type="button" data-lab-sample="sample2" aria-pressed="true">Hip</button><button type="button" data-lab-sample="sample5" aria-pressed="false">Knee*</button><button type="button" data-lab-sample="sample8" aria-pressed="false">Shoulder</button></div></div><div class="lab-comparison"><span class="eyebrow">FOUR TRAINING CONDITIONS</span><div id="lab-model-results" aria-live="polite">Choose a specimen to inspect its outputs.</div><p id="lab-label-note">Recorded FracAtlas knee labels are provisional and await clinician review.</p><a id="lab-open" href="demo.html?sample=2">Run this exact image live ↗</a></div></div></div></section>
<section id="workflow" class="workflow-section reference-section" data-tone="dark"><div class="wrap"><span class="eyebrow">04 · END-TO-END WORKFLOW</span><div class="workflow-layout"><div><h2>One complete pipeline.<br><em>Every step visible.</em></h2><p>Upload an X-ray or choose a sample. The workbench shows the expanded anatomy scores, four benchmark predictions and a Grad-CAM overlay.</p><div class="pipeline-states"><span>IMAGE SELECTED</span><span>VALIDATED</span><span>PREPROCESSED</span><span class="state-active">INFERENCE</span><span>COMPARED</span><span>VISUALIZED</span></div><a href="methodology.html">Explore the system architecture →</a></div><div class="workflow-card"><header><span class="state-dot"></span><b>Image → evidence</b><span>INTEGRATED</span></header><ol><li><span>01</span><div><b>Select or upload</b><p>JPEG, PNG, BMP, WebP or TIFF · up to 12 MB.</p></div></li><li><span>02</span><div><b>Prepare the input</b><p>Greyscale, 160 px and the recorded normalization.</p></div></li><li><span>03</span><div><b>Run the checkpoints</b><p>One six-region model and four benchmark checkpoints run locally on CPU.</p></div></li><li><span>04</span><div><b>Explain the comparison</b><p>Region scores and cutoffs, benchmark agreement, and the pooled checkpoint’s Grad-CAM overlay.</p></div></li></ol><div class="workflow-callout"><span>INPUT STAYS THE SAME</span><p>The checkpoints differ in their training sources. The report compares their joint predictions, scores and agreement.</p></div></div></div></div></section>
<section id="insight" class="insight-section reference-section" data-tone="mint"><div class="wrap insight-layout"><div><span class="eyebrow">05 · INSIGHT · SAVED BENCHMARK RESULTS</span><h2>Dimensions alone.</h2><div class="insight-number">{{dimension_gap}}<span>pp</span></div><p>drop in balanced accuracy when source is decoupled. The random forest uses only width, height and aspect ratio.</p><a class="btn primary" href="robustness.html">Ask the evidence →</a></div><div class="insight-cards"><article><span class="insight-icon">↗</span><h3>Pooled evaluation</h3><div><b>0.971</b><span>DIMENSIONS ONLY</span></div></article><article><span class="insight-icon">↘</span><h3>Source-controlled</h3><div><b>0.333</b><span>CHANCE LEVEL</span></div></article><article class="wide-insight"><span class="insight-icon">◎</span><h3>Fine-tuned EfficientNet-B3</h3><div><b>{{pooled}} <i>→</i> {{decoupled}}</b><span>BALANCED ACCURACY</span></div><p>All reported values come from saved project artifacts. Explore confidence intervals and the provisional-label limitations in Results.</p><a href="results.html">Inspect all models and intervals ↗</a></article></div></div></section>
